      "extract": "Four comments are in order. The first concerns the enumeration of the filtration. This follows from taking logs in ([\\[filter\\]](#filter){reference-type=\"ref\" reference=\"filter\"}), which gives $$\\log H(x,y)=-\\log(1-H_1(x)y)=-\\sum_{n,k} P_{n,k}\\log(1-x^n y^k)\\,. \\label{logs}$$ Equating coefficients of $y^j$, and setting $x=z^{1/j}$, we obtain $$^j=\\sum_{k|j} k P_k(z^{1/k}) \\label{classic}$$ which is a classic problem",
